body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The script reads and parses `runtimeSpineIn` and `querySurfacesIn` using `fs.readFileSync` and `JSON.parse` without any error handling or existence checks. If these critical artifacts are missing or malformed, the script will throw an unhandled exception and crash. Wrapping this in a `try-catch` block and returning a failed/blocked status ensures the script fails closed gracefully.

```javascript
  let runtimeSpine, querySurfaces;
  try {
    runtimeSpine = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, paths.runtimeSpineIn), 'utf8'));
    querySurfaces = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, paths.querySurfacesIn), 'utf8'));
  } catch (error) {
    blockersList.push(makeBlocker('critical_artifacts_missing_or_malformed', 'Critical input artifacts are missing or malformed: ' + error.message));
    return {
      status: 'blocked_local_env',
      target_type: 'local_disposable_supabase_postgres_database',
      supabase_status: statusParse.status,
      command_results: commandResults,
      blockers: blockersList,
      remote_fallback_attempted: false,
      remote_supabase_mutation_performed: false,
    };
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When loading critical input files (such as source maps), wrap the loading logic in a try-catch block to handle missing files, malformed JSON, non-object payloads, or non-array rows. Fail closed gracefully by returning an empty manifest, a validator failure status, a diagnostic code, and a readback instead of throwing unhandled exceptions.
</details>

