+function productionTranslationNotes(generatedAt) {
+  return `# KG-B1 Production Translation Notes
+
+Issue: #1290
+
+Generated at: ${generatedAt}
+
+## Boundary
+
+- This is a local/disposable Supabase rehearsal artifact only.
+- No production migration was created.
+- No remote Supabase mutation, remote seed, storage upload, or HTTP write probe is authorized by this issue.
+- No frontend route or public client integration is included.
+
+## Security Translation
+
+- Keep B1 views in a private or otherwise non-exposed schema unless a later human-approved production issue explicitly changes that boundary.
+- For Postgres 15 or newer, keep contract views as \`security_invoker = true\` so underlying table policies remain effective for the caller.
+- Keep RPC functions \`SECURITY INVOKER\` by default. Do not introduce \`SECURITY DEFINER\` for these query surfaces without a separate threat model and approval.
+- Data API exposure and RLS are separate controls. A production translation must define grants and RLS together instead of assuming either one implies the other.
+- Frontend clients must not receive service-role credentials. Any public runtime integration must use a narrower approved read model or backend-mediated access path.
+
+## Translation After Human Approval
+
+1. Recreate the B1 contract in a production migration draft after the B0 schema is approved.
+2. Replace local-only target guards with the repository's normal migration review path.
+3. Re-run count conservation against the approved target and compare the 3530/858/699/2672 gates.
+4. Add production RLS/grant tests before exposing any view or RPC outside private admin paths.
+`;
